  "raw_text": "167\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nwqu\n-\n02/20\n):\n \nJosep pamalika ra tuman l\nâ\nka ba nahki ambuk munan ki?\n \n–\n \nHow did envy harm Joseph’s family?\n \n/\n\n¿Cómo la envidia dañó a la familia de José?)\n\nAnsa munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto answer, to reply\n \n/ responder\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb-06/19\n):\n \nAisi\n \nkaiki ba ra, wan sinska ra naha makabi walanka nani ba ansa munaia sip sa “ya”, “d\nî\na”, “anira”,\n“ahkia”, “nahki”, bara “d\nî\na muni”.\n \n–\n \nIn the reading, in our mind we can answer the questions “who”, “what”, “where”,\n“when”, “how” and “why”.\n \n/ En la lectura, en nuestra mente podemos responder las preguntas \"quién\", \"qué\", \"dónde\",\n\"cuándo\", \"cómo\" y \"por qué\".)\n\nAparit munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto operate\n \n/ operar\n\nBut munaia\n \n(\nlv,rsg14\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto vote\n \n/ votar\n\nChens\n \n(a/t:\n \nSins\n)\n \nmunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto change, to cause change\n \n/ cambiar, causar cambio\n\n(Ex/Ej\n \n(\nlfb98\n):\n \nUpla ailal witin ra pain wali bara ai rayaka chens munan\n \n–\n \nMany people were listening (well) and changed\ntheir lives\n \n/ Muchas personas escuchaban (bueno) y cambiaron sus vidas)\n\nDanh munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto complete, to finish\n \n/ completar\n\nD\nî\na muni?\n \n–\n \nWhy?\n \n/ ¿Por qué?\n\nDruga yus munaia\n \n(\nfy,lv,bh\n,\nll\n; not in / no en:\n \ndict\n,\ndictu\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto use drugs\n \n/ usar drogas\n\nGrabar munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto record someone, to record something\n \n/ grabar a alguien, grabar algo\n\n(Note/Nota: from Spanish: Grabar / del español: Grabar)\n\nHilp munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto help, to aid\n \n/ ayudar\n\n(Note: In English, we would say\n \nhelp that person\n \n–\n \nnot\n \nhelp to that person.\n \nHowever, in Miskito, it is common to use\n \nra\n \nin\nthis way. Ex/Ej:\n \nYa disaipil takaia want nani ra hilp muns\n \n–\n \nHelp those who want to become disciples\n)\n\nHilp mamunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nministerial servant, helper\n \n/ siervo ministerial, ayudante\n\nKalik munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto collect\n \n/ recoger\n\nKlin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto clean\n \n/ limpiar\n\nKunin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto deceive someone, to trick someone, to lie to someone, to fool someone\n \n/ engañar a\nalguien, mentirle a alguien\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKunin munan\n \n–\n \nHe/she lied/tricked\n \n/ Él/ella mintió/engañó)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKunin wan munram\n \n–\n \nYou tricked us\n \n/ Nos engañaste)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nKunin ai munram\n \n–\n \nYou tricked me\n \n/ Me engañaste)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlfb60\n):\n \nKunin ai munaia trai kaikisma\n \n–\n \nYou are trying to trick me\n \n/ Estas tratando de engañarme)\n\nKunin mamunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nliar, deceiver\n \n/ mentiroso, engañador\n\nSwirka kunin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto allow to trick, to allow to be fooled\n \n/ permitir engañar, permitir ser\nengañado\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu-05/19-stadika21\n):\n \nYawan swika naha tasba sinska lâka mita kunin wan munbiara\n \n–\n \nDo not allow the\nwisdom of the world to fool us\n \n/ No permitas que la sabiduría del mundo nos engañe)\n\nLin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto lend\n \n/ prestar\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nLin ai muns...\n \n–\n \nLend me...\n \n/ Pr\né\nstame…\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \n100 kordoba nani lin ai munaia sip sma?\n \n–\n \nCan you lend me 100 cordobas?\n \n/ ¿Me puedes prestar 100 córdobas?\n)\n\nMamunra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \ndoer\n \n/ hacedor\n\n(Construct:\n \nMamunrika\n)\n\nMark munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto put a mark on something, to underline or put a note on something\n \n/ poner una marca en\n\nalgo, subrayar o poner una nota en algo\n\nMiks munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto mix\n \n/ mezclar\n\nMunbiara\n \n(v-alt-proh)\n \n–\n \nnot to do, do not do, we are not to do, one is not to do, we must not do, one must not do\n\n/ no hacer, no debemos hacer, uno no debe hacer\n\nMuni\n \n(v-present participle / presente participio)\n \n–\n \ndoing\n \n(usually to someone or something) / haciendo\n(generalmente a alguien o algo)\n\nMunka\n \n(a/t:\n \nMunrika\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsomething that one makes/causes another to do\n \n/ algo que uno hace que otro haga\n\n(Note/Nota: When this word is combined with a verb, it adds the idea of “to cause” or “to make”\n \n/ Cuando esta palabra se\ncombina con un verbo, agrega la idea de \"causar que\"\n \no “hacer\n \nque\n”\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Deut 7:4\n):\n \nWitin nani mita munka luhpiam nani Dawan wina tnaya ra tawi, gâd wala nani ra mayunbia\n \n–\n \nBy\nthem, your children will be made to be turning aside from the Lord to worship other gods\n \n/ Por ellos, sus hijos se\napartarán del Señor para adorar a otros dioses\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Lawana Nani 55:23\n):\n \nMan bui munrika raiti tihuka ra wabia\n \n–\n \nBy you, they will be made to go to the deep grave\n\n/ Por ti, serán hechos para ir a la tumba profunda)",
